  "hints": [
    "Almost everything is a write of a timestamped number. Which database is built for that?",
    "Buffer ingestion in a stream so a slow database never makes senders fail.",
    "LB (2) \u2192 Ingest API (20) \u2192 Kinesis \u2192 Time-Series DB (2), plus Ingest \u2192 Time-Series DB for dashboard reads."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 2200
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Time-series databases store data sorted by series and time, compress it heavily, and answer range queries fast.",
    "A stream (Kinesis, Kafka) absorbs bursts and lets several consumers (storage, alerting, anomaly detection) read the same data.",
    "Downsampling (keep 1-second data for a day, 1-minute for a month) keeps storage and dashboard queries cheap."
  ]
